// Single source of truth for BetterBLOX settings.
//
// Consumed by the standalone options page (betterblox-options/options.js),
// which imports the whole catalog and renders it without any dependency on the
// Roblox DOM. The legacy in-page settings UI that also read from here has been
// removed; the feature modules just read individual values at runtime via
// storageManager.getSettings(id, default) and no longer declare a settings map.
//
// Each setting: { type, id, title, description, defaultValue, isBeta? }
//   type "dropdown" also takes options: [{ value, label }]
//   type "input"    also takes placeholder?, maxLength?, width?

